\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A zero weight with a nonzero insertion}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Reduce #{K=2\bbI_2} from \ref{fdip-00TK} modulo #{4}.
Then
##{\det K=0,\qquad \adjugate K=2\bbI_2\ne0.}
For example,
#{\mathcal I_V(\psi_1\bar\psi_1\extexp(\theta_K))=2}.
Thus a singular configuration can contribute zero to the
partition coefficient and a nonzero value to an inserted
coefficient. Deleting it would change the functional.
The [unnormalized sum](fdip-00TU) and the complementary
minors in \ref{fdip-00TQ} remain defined; the
fixed-background inverse used in \ref{fdip-00TX} does not.}
